# Battery profiles: special-case the profile selector item in module
# 32's settings apply dispatch, decrement path. Companion to
# 0052-profile-selector-dispatch-b (the increment path runs a second
# copy of the dispatch; both copies need the special case). NOT in
# the manifest: unstacked until the module 32 segment extension build
# carries the profile blob at the branch target and the selector
# item record is authored (see gate).
name: profile-selector-dispatch-a
kind: module
module: 32
region: code
address: 0x0307deec
gate: build refuses unless the 6 stock bytes at the target equal
  `expect`; the finished image must also pass
  firmware_patch.validate(). Do NOT stack without the module 32
  segment extension carrying the battery-profile blob
  (work/power_build, linked at 0x030804ac, the first byte past
  module 32's stock code segment; the blob is appended with the
  framework --grow step, module 32 code). The cave target
  0x03080664 is inside that blob; if the blob's link base or layout
  changes, regenerate the branch bytes from src/sites.S.
rationale: Module 32's apply dispatch (disassembly in
  work/power_build/power_build.md) tests the item id, the descriptor
  halfword at [record + 8], at exec 0x0307dee4: 173 (0xad) takes the
  EQ path, 196 (0xc4) the brightness path, everything else the
  generic settings-changed post. The 6 bytes at this site are the
  second compare (cmp r0, #0xc4), its branch to the brightness path
  at 0x0307df84, and the fall-through branch to the generic exit at
  0x0307df8c. The replacement branches to the cave stub
  hook_dispatch_a at 0x03080664 in the module 32 extension. The stub
  re-executes the displaced compare and branch first, then tests
  the profile item id (0xc5; see the caveat in src/hooks.S: the id
  is a working value to confirm against the string table when the
  selector item record is authored), and on a match loads the
  record's value byte (the chosen profile, already updated by the
  stock value editor, exactly as items 173 and 196 consume it) and
  calls profile_select, which writes the profile area on first use
  and applies the profile. The stub exits through 0x0307df8c, the
  same generic post the site's own special cases fall into, so
  non-profile items are behaviour-identical to stock.
expect: c42849d04ce0
replace: 02f0babb00bf
